Have spoken to Key person in Nissan Motor and found as follows.

1) Target date for RFQ distribition is NOV19 as an outcome from Renault's meeting
2) Nissan has larger volume on ASIA-EUR trade and It is almost sure for Nissan to mainly control the trade on their tender,
however they still work on fixing role of Renault and Nissan by lane.
Further details won't be available until RFQ is given.
3) Indivisual negotiation has been ongoing. Nissan suggested target rate for 3 year contract to
7 carriers and now waiting for an outcome from each carrier.
4) Target rate can not be disclosed to others than designated carrier.

5) Specific lanes included in open tender will vary by results of indivisual negotiation.



Though we are not listed in an indivisual negotiation carrier, submitted our wish list of lanes where we want to be involved in next 3 years.

We will continue to seek through communication with Nissan for further details and any hints to form our strategy.



