Subject: Renault Tender Kick Off Meeting Minutes


To: XCGs, XSGs, XCMs, CCM, CCE, CCB, CCA. , LEHBBG/S, TYOBB
Fm: UCM

Dear all,

Please find below minutes of the information meeting held at Renault in Paris introducing their tender process.

Location
Guyancourt (Paris), France October 30th 2013
Attendees
Renault/Nissan: Jean-Elophe Blaise, Logistics Suppliers MGR for Europe
Renault/Nissan: Carl Beijer, Logistics Supplier
Renault/Nissan: Kumi Yoshida, Logistics Buyer
Renault: Vincent Rome, Overseas transport MGR
Renault: Frederic Depaepe, Project Leader transport
Renault: Loup Tournand, Project Leader transport
HJS: LEHBBG, BBS, BBS/Yun-Ho Frere, UCG/Rob Durenkamp, UCM

Other shipping lines were invited at the same time, as this was a group session.

Basic tender process overview


  *   17 carriers are invited
  *   Schedule:

     *   RFQ release: Nov. 19th
     *   1 round offer: Dec. 12th
     *   1 round F2F: W4 2014
     *   2 round offer: W5 2014
     *   2 round F2F: W6
     *   Nomination: Early March 2014

  *   Tender contents:

     *   3 year rate validity for routes covering "mature", or "steady" markets (such as AESW, TPSE)
     *   1 year validity for "volatile" or "emerging" markets (such as Latam)
     *   a SLA (Service Level Agreement)

  *   Potential volumes: More than 310,000 TEUs per year (1/3 for Renault, rest for Nissan)

*         Renault/Nissan negotiation parties are split between Paris and Tokyo:

     *   Europe to/from Latam: Paris
     *   Other trades: Tokyo

  *   Bidding platforms:

     *   Paris negotiated portion: OCCON
     *   Tokyo negotiated portion: Excel sheets

  *   Selection criteria:

     *   O/F level
     *   Transit time (no T/S, 1 additional day transit time is valued at a cost of USD 20/25)
     *   There will be a floating mechanism, but not yet fixed, probably a BAF reviewed every 6 months
     *   7 to 10 carrier globally will be selected

  *   There are also 3 or 4 port/pairs that dont fall under the 1 or 3 year validity tenders. They will be follow a more simple RFQ process



A presentation of the bid will be distributed in the coming days, i will forward it to relevant parties as soon as received.

Similar presentation will be held in Japan.



UCM recommendations:



As per Renault/Nissan's set up of having 2 negotiation parties, it is difficult to have 1 internal Customer Management team

to handle this customer. However as per their split of trades, HJS has the most potential and interest in the Tokyo negotiated part. For the Paris negotiated part, HJS allocation and service is limited.

Therefore, would suggest that ASM takes over the lead on this customer in collaboration with TYOBB.

LEHBB will remain as contact window for the Paris part.



Kind Regards,

UCM


